* "American Lead C+" preamp: a dual-channel, five-stage lead amp of the late 1970s / 1980s (the Mark IIC+, from the user's drawing "Mark IIC+ Schematic FINAL.pdf",
* RP10A / RP11A boards; the drawing's component numbers are not official). Rhythm: V1A, tone stack, volume 1, V1B, V2B, V2A, master. Lead: the same V1A / V1B / tone
* stack, then V3B (lead drive) and V4A into V2B's grid, with the lead master after V2B. The channel, the pull switches and the treble shift are light-dependent
* resistors on the original (LDR1A..LDR4A): here switches (selectors) that are 1 ohm (1 k for an LDR) or open (1e12).
* Not modelled: the spring reverb (V3A, V4B, tank), the five-band graphic EQ, the C++ mods (dashed on the drawing), C27 and the 120 pF on V2A (removed on later amps).
* Component values as drawn; where the drawing gives two (RP10A / RP11A) the RP11A (later) one.

* Rail D (node X): driven from the power amp at run time; D+ is behind R86 (1k) and C87.
V VRAIL x 100 450
R R86 x dp 1k
C C87 dp 0 30u

* The guitar and its pickup / cable networks (the engine closes these switches), V1A with its two cathode bypass paths.
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p

R R1 in 0 1M
T V1A in p1 k1 12AX7
R R4 dp p1 150k
R R2 k1 0 1.5k
C C1 k1 0 0.47u
* C2 with R3 (15k); the PULL SHIFT BASS switch grounds C2 directly.
C C2 k1 c2n 22u
R R3 c2n 0 15k
R SW_SHIFT c2n 0 1e12

* Tone stack: 250p to the treble pot, 100k slope, .1u (bass) and .047u (middle) from the slope node. TREBLE SHIFT adds 750p (C6) across the treble feed.
C C5 p1 t0 250p
C C6 p1 xs 750p
R R6 xs t0 10M
R SW_TSHIFT xs t0 1e12
R R5 p1 sl 100k
R VR3T t0 w3 1
R VR3B w3 b1 1
C C4 sl b1 0.1u
R VR5 b1 m1 125k
C C3 sl m1 0.047u
R VR4 m1 0 5k

* Volume 1 (1M) behind the optional 100k, the PULL BRIGHT 180p across it, V1B.
R R_OPT w3 vt 100k
R VR1T vt w 1
R VR1B w 0 1
C C_BR vt cb 180p
R SW_BR cb w 1e12
T V1B w p1b k1b 12AX7
R R8 dp p1b 100k
R R7 k1b 0 1.5k
C C13 k1b 0 22u

* V1B's plate: C7 into the node that feeds both channels (R9 to ground); the rhythm path to V2B's grid is 10p parallel 3.3M.
C C7 p1b nr 0.1u
R R9 nr 0 100k
C C10 nr g2b 10p
R R10 nr g2b 3.3M

* Lead channel: C21 and the lead input switch (LDR2A), R21, LEAD DRIVE (1M) into V3B; V3B -> C25, R25 (270k) with R24 (68k) / C24 (1000p) -> V4A.
C C21 nr li0 0.02u
R SW_LI li0 li1 1e12
R R21 li1 li 680k
R VR_LDT li ld 1
R VR_LDB ld 0 1
T V3B ld p3b k3b 12AX7
R R22 ld 0 475k
C C22 ld k3b 120p
R R23 k3b 0 1.5k
C C23 k3b 0 2.2u
R R26 dp p3b 82k
C C25 p3b a25 0.022u
R R25 a25 g4a 270k
C C24 g4a 0 1000p
R R24 g4a 0 68k
T V4A g4a p4a k4a 12AX7
R R27 dp p4a 274k
R R30 k4a 0 3.3k
* C29 with R29 (6.8k); the PULL BRIGHT LEAD MASTER switch grounds C29 directly.
C C29 k4a c29 0.22u
R R29 c29 0 6.8k
R SW_BL c29 0 1e12
C C30 p4a q 0.047u
R R31 q lo 220k
C C31 q lo 250p
R R32 lo 0 100k
C C32 lo 0 500p
* The lead output switch (LDR3A) into V2B's grid.
R SW_LO lo g2b 1e12

* V2B: R11 / C11 on the grid, 1.5k unbypassed cathode, plate R13; R105 and C9 to the LEAD MASTER (a 250k rheostat to ground through LDR4A, lead only).
T V2B g2b p2b k2b 12AX7
R R11 g2b 0 680k
C C11 g2b 0 47p
R R13 x p2b 100k
R R16 k2b 0 1.5k
R R105 p2b r105 47k
C C9 r105 m1o 0.047u
R VR_LM m1o lm1 125k
R SW_LM lm1 0 1e12

* Effects loop (R102 / R101 divider, send / return jacks closed, R12) into V2A, whose cathode has 1k with .47u and 22u (R20 68k, GAIN BOOST grounds it).
R R102 m1o mm 150k
R R101 mm 0 4.7k
R R12 mm g2a 2.2k
R R103 g2a 0 47k
T V2A g2a p2a k2a 12AX7
R R19 x p2a 120k
R R104 k2a 0 1k
C C16 k2a 0 0.47u
C C15 k2a c15 22u
R R20 c15 0 68k
R SW_BOOST c15 0 1e12

* Output: C12, R106 (15k), then the MASTER (1M rheostat to ground). The power amp's input lives in poweramp.net.
C C12 p2a y1 0.047u
R R106 y1 y 15k
R VR_M y 0 500k
